              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "<div class=\"description\">\n\"Javanese Landscape, with Tigers Listening to the Sound of a Travelling Group\" was completed by Raden Saleh in Dresden, the cultural centre of Saxony, and presented to his patron and friend His Highness Ernest II, Duke of Saxe- Coburg and Gotha, in 1849. The painting was in the family for many years as it was inherited by the second son, grandson and great-grandson of Queen Victoria and Prince Albert.</div>",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
